{
  "id": "y9-algorithms-l7",
  "label": "9CT.01 L7: Iteration - Plant a Whole Strip",
  "steps": [
    {"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Selection Retrieval","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l7_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Selection Retrieval</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Quick recall from last lesson.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-a\">(a) What instruction ends every IF block?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-b\">(b) With ELSE, how many of the two branches ever run?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"title","label":"Iteration: Plant a Whole Strip","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithms and Data</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Iteration: Plant a Whole Strip</h2><p>Year 9, 9CT.01</p></div>"},
    {"id":"objectives","label":"Three Goals","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Three Goals</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Repeat</h3><p>Use <code>FOR ... TO ... NEXT</code> to repeat a known number of times.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Count</h3><p>Understand what the loop variable actually holds on each pass.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Reuse</h3><p>Use the loop variable itself inside an action, like <code>SetPosition</code>.</p></div></div>"},
    {"id":"direct-instruction","label":"FOR Syntax","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">FOR Syntax</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A <strong>FOR loop</strong> repeats its lines a fixed, known number of times.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Step &lt;- 1 TO 3</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Buy(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Step</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>No colon and no &quot;DO&quot; on a FOR line.</li><li>A FOR loop ends with <code>NEXT</code> followed by the <strong>same</strong> variable name.</li><li><code>Step</code> takes the values 1, 2, then 3 in turn - three passes, not four.</li><li>Use the loop variable inside an action to make each pass genuinely different, e.g. <code>CALL SetPosition(Step, 0)</code>.</li></ul>"},
    {"id":"worked-check","label":"Check: Trace the Loop","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l7_worked_check","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Trace the Loop</h2><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Step &lt;- 0 TO 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL SetPosition(Step, 0)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Buy(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Plant(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Step</div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-a\">(a) How many times does CALL Plant run in total?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-b\">(b) List the three values Step takes, in order.</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-worked-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"farmer-tutorial","label":"Machine Tutorial: Strip Farm","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y9-algorithms-l7-farmer-button","appId":"pseudocodefarmer","appQuery":"tutorial=strip-farm","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Machine Tutorial: Strip Farm</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Open Pseudocode Farmer. It will take you straight into the Strip Farm tutorial - follow every step in order.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Complete when</h3><p>The tutorial panel says &quot;Tutorial complete&quot; and three Carrots are planted in a row from a single Run.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-farmer-button\">Open Pseudocode Farmer</button></div>"},
    {"id":"scaffold-fill-blank","label":"Fix the Range","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l7-fill-blank","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l7_fill_blank","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Fix the Range</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This loop is meant to buy exactly 5 Potato seeds, but it only buys 4.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Step &lt;- 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Buy(&quot;Potato&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Step</div></div><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-fill-blank-a\">Rewrite the FOR line only, so it buys exactly 5 seeds.</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-fill-blank-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-fill-blank-a\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-fill-blank-button\">Check answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-fill-blank-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"independent-task","label":"Independent Task: Four Tomatoes","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l7-independent","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l7_independent","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Independent Task: Four Tomatoes</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Write your own FOR loop from scratch. No walkthrough this time.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Requirement</h3><p>Write a FOR loop, using the loop variable <code>Slot</code>, that buys exactly 4 Tomato seeds.</p></div><div class=\"pseudocode-check\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-independent-code\"><strong>Your loop</strong></label><textarea id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-independent-code\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-independent-code\" spellcheck=\"false\" rows=\"5\"></textarea><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-independent-check\">Check my answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-independent-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div></div>"},
    {"id":"extension","label":"Extension: WHILE Loops","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y9-algorithms-l7-extension-button","appId":"pseudocodefarmer","appQuery":"tutorial=stock-up-run","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Extension: WHILE Loops</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">FOR is for when you know the count in advance. What if you don't - you just want to keep going for as long as something is true? Try the Stock-Up Run tutorial to see a <code>WHILE ... DO ... ENDWHILE</code> loop for the first time.</p><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-extension-button\">Open Pseudocode Farmer</button></div>"},
    {"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Iteration","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l7_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Iteration</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-a\">(a) What instruction ends a FOR loop?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-b\">(b) FOR Count &lt;- 1 TO 6 - how many times does the loop run?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l7-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Next lesson: <strong>Nested Iteration</strong> - a loop inside a loop, to plant a whole grid.</p>"}
  ],
  "validators": {
    "y9_algorithms_l7_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*endif\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Every IF block closes with ENDIF."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(?:exactly\\s*)?one\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Exactly one branch runs - THEN or ELSE, never both, never neither."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l7_worked_check":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*3\\s*(?:times)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The loop body runs once per pass, and TO 2 starting at 0 means 3 passes."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"0.*1.*2","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Step starts at 0 and counts up to 2: 0, then 1, then 2."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l7_fill_blank":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"for\\s*step\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*1\\s*to\\s*5","flags":"i"},"feedback":"1 TO 4 only gives 4 passes (1, 2, 3, 4) - change the 4 to a 5."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l7_independent":[{"suffix":"code","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"for\\s*slot\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*1\\s*to\\s*4[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*buy\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']tomato[\"']\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*?next\\s*slot","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Check the range (1 TO 4 gives 4 passes), the crop (Tomato), and that NEXT names the same variable, Slot."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l7_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*next\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"A FOR loop ends with NEXT and the loop variable's name."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*6\\s*(?:times)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"1 TO 6 counts 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 - six passes."}]
  }
}
